WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.369
Charlotte Mason was a 19th century British educator

1
00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:06.570
who believed that education is an atmosphere,

2
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.650
a discipline,

3
00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:08.710
a life.

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.329
Rather than relying on the traditional textbooks of the time,

5
00:00:12.609 --> 00:00:15.819
her approach centers on what she called living books,

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.629
narrative works written with passion by subject matter experts

7
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.719
that bring topics such as history,

8
00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:22.489
science,

9
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.069
and literature to life.

10
00:00:24.479 --> 00:00:25.879
To process information,

11
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.899
students use narration,

12
00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:30.709
retellings of what they just read or heard,

13
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.790
which builds deep comprehension,

14
00:00:32.909 --> 00:00:33.819
vocabulary,

15
00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:35.259
and active listening.

16
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.779
Lessons are kept short,

17
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.159
typically 15 to 30 minutes,

18
00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:43.380
to form habits of focused attention and to prevent mental fatigue.

19
00:00:43.759 --> 00:00:45.990
The method also features nature study,

20
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.119
picture and music appreciation,

21
00:00:48.409 --> 00:00:49.040
copy work,

22
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.299
and handcrafts,

23
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.360
creating a rich,

24
00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:53.159
broad feast of learning.

25
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.759
By focusing on habit formation and noble ideas,

26
00:00:57.009 --> 00:00:59.569
the Charlotte Mason approach aims to cultivate a

27
00:00:59.569 --> 00:01:02.270
lifelong love of learning in every child.